@module landscape ; The landscape generator
@about NewLandscape from the five-digit gene: the map all water, land discs at random centres and radii, tree discs on land, then the coast from the eight-neighbour patterns. MapAddr and MapAddrChecked, the map's address arithmetic, live here.
$6A8C w Gene 1 ; The landscape's gene, the seed of the generator (3 in the image: "00003")

$6A8E c NewLandscape ; Make the landscape from Gene: the map all water, 128 land discs, the coasts, 32 tree discs
> Resets the simulation (StartSimulation $830C), clears CityMap $C450 to 0 (water), shows "CREATING LANDSCAPE" ($A6A4), seeds Random with Gene, draws 128 discs of land ($02) with radius 2-7 at x, y 16-79 (Disc), cuts the coast (MakeCoast), then 32 discs of trees ($06) of radius 2-3 drawn only over land. L1 12 (the menus recording's genes 12345 and 00003, the level starts).

$6AD3 b DiscShapes 2 ; Four pairs of shifts (4, 4), (5, 3), (3, 5), (4, 4): the disc's two axes (round, flat, tall)
@res tables/DiscShapes.bin

$6ADB c Discs ; B discs of cell C, radius 2 to E (random), centre 16-79, each with a random shape from DiscShapes
$6AE3 DiscsLoop
$6AEF DiscsRadius

$6B21 b CoastPatterns 33 ; The coast: 66 masks of the eight land neighbours, then the 66 cell codes put on such water
> Read by MakeCoast with CPIR (L1 426 157 compares).
@res tables/Coast.bin
$6B63 CoastCells ; the cell code for each pattern

