@module saveload ; Save and load
@about SAVE TO TAPE and LOAD FROM TAPE: a 31-byte header and the 9216-byte map, both with flag $FF, through the ROM.
$9E09 c SaveCity ; SAVE TO TAPE: the name, START TAPE, then a 31-byte header (flag $FF) and the 9216-byte map (flag $FF)
> The header SaveHeader: the 12-letter file name, Funds, its spare byte, Month, Year (7 bytes), a spare byte, the city name (12). Nothing else is saved: not the tax, the fundings, the options or the arrays. Known only from the code (stage 1's save recording ran it: L1 at $9E09 none, as the save was reached through the menu action; see NOTES).
$9E5A c LoadCity ; LOAD FROM TAPE: the name, SEARCHING, a 31-byte header (any name if the typed one is blank), then the map; only the first city on the tape loads
> Both blocks of a save carry flag $FF, and LoadHeader asks for 31 bytes with flag $FF. After a header whose name does not match, the next load meets that file's map block, takes its first 31 bytes as a header, fails the parity (the block is longer) and shows LoadErrorWindow: the search never reaches a second file, so the tape must stand at the wanted city. Known only from the code.
> PopLastYear and LastPop are not restored: the previous city's values remain until the next month end.
$9E77 b SearchingText 18 ; PrintInline codes: a box, SEARCHING
@res text/inline/Searching.bin
$9E89 c LoadHeader
$9EA0 LoadHeaderBlank
$9EAA LoadHeaderCompare
$9EB3 LoadHeaderLoop
$9EBE LoadHeaderMatch
$9EC1 b LoadingText 11 ; PrintInline: LOADING
@res text/inline/Loading.bin
$9ECC c LoadMap ; The map; on success Funds, the date and the name from the header
$9EFC LoadMapFailed ; a bad map: the error window, then a new city
$9F0C LoadHeaderFailed
$9F1A c PrintFound ; FOUND :- and the header's name
$9F1D b FoundText 13
@res text/inline/Found.bin
$9F2A c PrintFileName ; The 12 letters at SaveName
$9F2F PrintFileNameLoop

@module dialogs ; The menus' descriptions and actions, the line editor
@about The SYSTEM, OPTIONS, DISASTERS and WINDOWS menus, the dialogs (confirm, about, load, save, file name, tape, speed, level, old landscape) and their actions; the options' flags; the name and gene editor.
$9F40 b PlantChoice 1 ; The power station menu's answer: 0 none, 1 nuclear, 2 coal
$9F41 b PlantMenu 16 ; the menu: SELECT TYPE, NUCLEAR POWER STATION $5000, COAL POWER STATION $3000, NONE
@res text/menus/Plant.bin include
$9FBE c NoPlant ; NONE: PlantChoice 0 (not run in the recordings)
$9FC4 c ChooseNuclear ; PlantChoice 1
> L1 3.
$9FCA ChooseCoal ; PlantChoice 2
$9FD0 c Confirm ; ARE YOU SURE ?: carry set for YES
> L1 5.
$9FD3 b ConfirmMenu 16
@res text/menus/Confirm.bin include
$A027 c ConfirmNo ; OR A
$A029 ConfirmYes ; SCF
$A02B b SystemMenu 16 ; SYSTEM: about, start new city, use old landscape, load, save, exit
@res text/menus/System.bin include
$A0B1 c ExitSimCity ; EXIT SIMCITY: confirmed, a new city with a new landscape
$A0B7 NewCityItem ; START NEW CITY: confirmed, the gene from the random seed, then NewCity
$A0C1 NewCity ; the difficulty menu, then NewLandscape
$A0C7 c AboutWindow ; ABOUT SIM CITY
$A0CA b AboutText 16
@res text/menus/About.bin include
$A1F3 c LoadMenu ; LOADING MENU
$A1F6 b LoadMenuText 16
@res text/menus/Load.bin include
$A247 c SaveMenu ; SAVING MENU
$A24A b SaveMenuText 16
@res text/menus/Save.bin include
$A29A c FileNameWindow ; TYPE FILE NAME, THEN PRESS ENTER
$A29D b FileNameText 16
@res text/menus/FileName.bin include
$A2DC c LoadErrorWindow ; TAPE LOADING ERROR
$A2DF b LoadErrorText 16
@res text/menus/LoadError.bin include
$A2FE c WaitTapeStart ; START TAPE AND PRESS SPACE: wait for SPACE
$A301 WaitTapeLoop
$A303 WaitTapeIn
$A305 WaitTapeTest
$A307 WaitTapeAgain
$A309 c TapeWindow
$A30C b TapeText 16
@res text/menus/Tape.bin include
$A32B b AutoBulldoze 1 ; the options (toggles): AUTO-BULLDOZE 1, AUTO-BUDGET 0, SOUND 1, ZONE DEMOLISH WAIT 1
$A32C AutoBudget
$A32D SoundOn
$A32E DemolishWait
$A32F b OptionsMenu 16 ; OPTIONS: the four toggles, SIMULATION SPEED, EXIT MENU
@res text/menus/Options.bin include
$A3AB b Speed 1 ; 0 fast, 1 normal, 2 slow, 3 paused
$A3AC c SpeedMenu ; SIMULATION SPEED
$A3AF b SpeedMenuText 16
@res text/menus/Speed.bin include
$A3D0 SpeedMarkFast ; the asterisk places of the four items
$A3DB SpeedMarkNormal
$A3E8 SpeedMarkSlow
$A3F3 SpeedMarkPaused
$A40D c SetSpeedItem ; Speed = A; the asterisk moved to (HL)
$A421 SpeedFast
$A428 SpeedNormal
$A42F SpeedSlow
$A436 SpeedPaused
$A43D b DisastersOff 1 ; DISABLE ALL (a toggle): no random disasters
$A43E b DisasterMenu 16 ; DISASTERS: fire, flood, earthquake, air crash, tornado, nuclear meltdown
@res text/menus/Disasters.bin include
$A4BA c PickDisaster ; DisasterDue = the item + 1
> L1 6.
$A4C2 b WindowsMenu 16 ; WINDOWS: maps, budget, evaluation
@res text/menus/Windows.bin include
$A511 b MapsDue 1 ; set by MAPS: the UI task opens the maps window
$A512 c MapsItem
$A518 b Level 1 ; 0 easy, 1 medium, 2 difficult
$A519 c LevelMenu ; SELECT DIFFICULTY LEVEL
$A51C b LevelMenuText 16
@res text/menus/Level.bin include
$A5A9 c SetLevel ; Level = the item
> L1 12.
$A5B0 InputCityName ; INPUT NEW CITY NAME: edit CityName at row 5
$A5DC UseOldLandscape ; USE OLD LANDSCAPE: the gene into the menu's number, the menu
$A5E5 b OldLandscapeMenu 16
@res text/menus/OldLandscape.bin include
$A61B GeneShown ; the gene in the menu (code 6's value)
$A672 c InputGene ; INPUT NEW GENE: 5 digits at row 11, column 25
$A68C InputGeneShow
$A6A4 b CreatingText 16 ; CREATING LANDSCAPE, PLEASE WAIT
@res text/menus/Creating.bin include
$A6D8 b InputAt 2 ; the line editor: row, column, the buffer, the cursor, the digits flag, the length, a buffer of 12, the key delay
$A6DA InputBuffer
$A6DC InputCursor
$A6DD InputDigits
$A6DE InputLength
$A6DF InputText
$A6EF InputDelay

$A6F9 c InputName ; Edit an 11-letter text at InputAt (InputLength = 11: CityName's twelfth letter cannot be typed) (letters, digits, space; CAPS SHIFT 5 / 8 cursor, 0 blanks the cursor cell and the one before it)
$A6FF c InputLine ; The line editor; with InputDigits a number (5 digits, carry when too large)
> L1 5.
$A70A InputLoop
$A725 InputKey
$A742 InputChar
$A751 InputPrintable
$A756 InputDrop
$A757 InputNoKey
$A75D InputShow
$A762 InputRepeat
$A76D InputPut
$A77D InputDelete
$A786 c InputBlank ; A space at the cursor
$A793 c CursorLeft
$A799 CursorRight
$A7A3 c ShowInput ; The text at InputAt, the cursor's letter inverse ($C7)
$A7B6 ShowInputLoop
$A7C2 ShowInputChar
$A7D4 c NumberToInput ; The 16-bit number at (InputBuffer) as digits into InputText
$A7EB w NumberAt 1
$A7ED c NumberDigits
$A81E c NumberDigit
$A823 NumberDigitLoop
$A82A c PutDigit
$A834 NumberDigitSkip
$A836 InputEnter ; ENTER: a number is converted and stored (carry: none or too large)
$A849 c DigitValue ; A = E - '0', carry when E is not a digit
$A854 c InputToNumber ; HL = the decimal digits of InputText, carry on overflow
$A85B InputToNumberLoop
$A882 InputToNumberOver

@module workspace ; The movers' sprites and the work space
@about The five 16 x 16 sprites, the save header, and the arrays built at run time: the fire and police coverage, pollution, traffic, the power bitmap and the 96 x 96 city map.
$A884 b MoverSprites 2 ; The movers' 16 x 16 sprites, 32 bytes each: the plane, two tornado frames, the train across and down
@res graphics/Movers.bin
$A924 t SaveName 12 ; The name typed for LOAD and SAVE
$A930 b SaveHeader 16 ; The tape header (31 bytes): file name 12, Funds 3, a spare, Month, Year 2, a spare, the city name 11 (SaveCityName $A944-$A94E)
$A93C SaveFunds
$A944 SaveCityName
$A94F b SaveSpare 1 ; The city name's twelfth letter: SaveCity copies 12 letters to $A944, but the header block ends at $A94E, so this byte never reaches the tape; LoadCity copies it back from RAM
$A950 s FireCover 576 ; The 24 x 24 fire coverage, 0-15 (zero in the image: built at run time)
$AB90 s PoliceCover 576 ; The 24 x 24 police coverage, 0-15
$ADD0 s Pollution 2304 ; The 48 x 48 pollution, 0-255
$B6D0 s Traffic 2304 ; The 48 x 48 traffic, 0-$F0
$BFD0 s PowerMap 1152 ; The powered bit of each map cell, 12 bytes a row
$C450 s CityMap 9216 ; The 96 x 96 map, all land (2) in the image: NewLandscape makes it

@module graphics ; The tiles and their attributes
@about IconTiles, CellTiles and BuildingTiles (8 bytes a tile) and their attribute tables.
$E850 b IconTiles 8 ; The 67 icon and frame tiles, 8 bytes each: the tool palette (2 x 2 each), the frames $38-$3F, the separators $40-$42
@res graphics/IconTiles.bin
$EA68 b CellTiles 8 ; The 94 cell tiles of the map (cells 0-$5D; $5A-$5D the fire and flood frames AnimateFire and AnimateFlood copy)
@res graphics/CellTiles.bin
$ED58 b BuildingTiles 8 ; The 244 building tiles (a building row's tile numbers n, n + 1, ...)
@res graphics/BuildingTiles.bin
$F4F8 b IconAttrs 8 ; The attributes of icons 0-55 (DrawIcon reads IconAttrs + A; the frame tiles use PrintAttr)
@res graphics/IconAttrs.bin
$F530 b CellAttrs 8 ; The cells' attributes
@res graphics/CellAttrs.bin
$F58E b BuildingAttrs 8 ; The building tiles' attributes
@res graphics/BuildingAttrs.bin
@module tasks ; The task switcher
@about The two tasks' stacks and frame, the switch state (TaskNow, SwitchOff) and Interrupt, the IM 2 handler. The vector table $FD00 and the jump $FCFC are at the end of the system module (a module is one stretch of addresses).
$F682 s UiStack 64 ; The UI task's stack: Entry sets SP = $F6C2 (UiStack+$40); written down to $F68A (menus frame 3466), 8 bytes above BuildingAttrs
$F6C2 s SimStack 44 ; The simulation task's stack below SimFrame: it grows down from $F704 into SimFrame and below; written down to $F6D0 (menus frame 5498); $F6C2-$F6CF never written
$F6EE b SimFrame 20 ; The simulation task's first frame: 20 bytes of registers, then the entry
$F702 w SimEntry 1 ; SimTask: the first switch returns into it
$F704 b TaskNow 1 ; 0 the UI task runs, 1 the simulation
$F705 b SwitchOff 1 ; Nonzero: the interrupt does not switch tasks (the UI's critical parts)
$F706 SwitchSpare
$F707 w UiSP 1 ; the stacks of the two tasks while the other runs
$F709 SimSP

$F70B c Interrupt ; IM 2: save all registers, ReadInput, then (unless SwitchOff) swap the stack with the other task's
> Each interrupt, 50 a second, gives the other task the CPU: the UI and the simulation run turn by turn, one frame each. c1: L1 407 762, 128 197 / 256 388 switches.
$F733 InterruptToSim
$F73B InterruptFlip
$F73E InterruptReturn
@module system ; Printing glyphs, the input read, the tape, the $E5 leftover and the IM 2 vector
@about PrintGlyph with the print state, ReadInput (keys and joysticks every interrupt), TapeLoad, TapeSave, TapePause, 1345 leftover $E5 bytes, InterruptJump $FCFC and the vector table $FD00.
$F74E b PrintCharCode 1 ; The print state: the character, the screen address, the column and row, the attribute
> PrintCharCode is written by PrintDigit and read by nobody (PrintGlyph takes the code in A).
$F74F PrintAddr
$F751 PrintCol
$F752 PrintRow
$F753 PrintAttr
$F754 c PrintGlyph ; Character A from the ROM font, made bold (byte OR byte >> 1), at PrintAddr, with PrintAttr unless $FF
> L1 496 214.
$F764 PrintGlyphLine
$F76E PrintGlyphAttr
$F774 PutAttr
$F781 c ReadInput ; Read the eight half rows into KeyRows, then the Kempston and Sinclair joysticks into them
> L1 413 183.
$F789 ReadInputRow
$F798 b ReadInputLeftover 7 ; Leftover: RET, JP $FE0F, JP $FE0F (no code runs them)
$F79F c TapeLoad ; LD-BYTES through the ROM (border $0F): IX, DE, A flag, carry set
$F7AA c TapeSave ; SA-BYTES through the ROM
$F7AD c TapePause ; B x 5000 loops
$F7B1 TapePauseLoop
$F7BB s E5Fill 1345 ; Leftover: 1345 bytes of $E5 (the byte a CP/M or +3DOS format writes); no stack or code touches them (L1: untouched)
$FCFC c InterruptJump ; JP Interrupt: the IM 2 vector $FCFC
$FCFF b InterruptSpare 1
$FD00 VectorTable ; 257 bytes $FC: with I = $FD any vector reads $FCFC
